MODULE: posts/api
FILES: src/app/api/posts/route.ts, src/app/api/posts/[id]/route.ts, src/app/api/categories/route.ts, src/app/api/categories/[id]/route.ts, src/app/api/tags/route.ts, src/app/api/tags/[id]/route.ts, src/lib/slugify.ts
RESPONSIBILITY: post CRUD API, categories/tags CRUD API with validation, slug utility
KEY_FILES:
- src/app/api/posts/route.ts: GET list with pagination/filtering/sorting, POST create with auth
- src/app/api/posts/[id]/route.ts: GET/PUT/DELETE single post with auth, cascade delete
- src/app/api/categories/route.ts: GET categories with post counts, POST create with auth/validation
- src/app/api/categories/[id]/route.ts: GET/PUT/DELETE single category with auth, disassociates posts on delete
- src/app/api/tags/route.ts: GET tags with post counts, POST create with auth/validation
- src/app/api/tags/[id]/route.ts: GET/PUT/DELETE single tag with auth, PostTag cascade on delete
- src/lib/slugify.ts: URL-friendly slug generation from title
DEPENDENCIES:
- uses: next-auth: getServerSession for API auth
- uses: @prisma/client: ORM queries with includes and _count
- imports: src/lib/prisma: Prisma singleton
- imports: src/lib/slugify: slugify function
INTERFACES:
- GET /api/posts: list with ?page, ?limit, ?status, ?sortBy, ?sortOrder — returns {posts, pagination}
- POST /api/posts: create post — requires auth, body: {title, content, slug?, excerpt?, coverImageUrl?, categoryId?, tags?, status?}
- GET /api/posts/[id]: read single post with category, tags, author
- PUT /api/posts/[id]: update post — requires auth, partial body
- DELETE /api/posts/[id]: delete post — requires auth, cascades to PostTag and Comment
- GET /api/categories: list all categories with _count.posts
- POST /api/categories: create category — requires auth, body: {name}, validates 1-50 chars, auto-slug, unique check
- GET /api/categories/[id]: read single category with post count
- PUT /api/categories/[id]: update category — requires auth, body: {name}, validates uniqueness
- DELETE /api/categories/[id]: delete category — requires auth, sets post.categoryId to null first
- GET /api/tags: list all tags with _count.posts
- POST /api/tags: create tag — requires auth, body: {name}, validates 1-50 chars, auto-slug
- GET /api/tags/[id]: read single tag with post count
- PUT /api/tags/[id]: update tag — requires auth, body: {name}, validates uniqueness
- DELETE /api/tags/[id]: delete tag — requires auth, PostTag entries cascade-deleted
TRAPS:
- [LOW] Session user id accessed via (session.user as {id?: string}).id cast — next-auth default type lacks id field | FIX: cast to {id?: string} in all API routes
- [LOW] slugify uses regex replace chain — may not handle unicode/emoji correctly | FIX: acceptable for English-only blog content
- [LOW] Category delete disassociates posts before deleting — two DB operations not in a transaction | FIX: acceptable for single-user blog, low concurrency
CHANGELOG:
- root | add: initial posts API with CRUD, pagination, filtering, sorting
- F-004 | add: categories CRUD API with post counts, validation, post disassociation
- F-004 | add: tags CRUD API with post counts, validation, cascade delete
